summer is around the corner and it's  time to make sure your home is  conserving water and following the  mandatory watering restrictions here's a  reminder from the southern nevada water  authority the sponsors of this segment  [Music]  i'm diana diaz with the southern nevada  water authority here to tell you about  the watering restrictions for summer the  mandatory summer watering restrictions  are in effect may through august which  means that you cannot water any day  between 11 am and 7 pm sunday watering  is prohibited year round it's  recommended that you water in the early  morning hours to avoid water loss to  evaporation or daytime winds  also slowly ramp up the number of days  that you water your grass in the summer  maintaining a three to four day weekly  watering schedule and adding additional  days as the summer heat increases will  help you reduce water use  save on your water bill and maintain a  healthy landscape to avoid over watering  water your grass no more than 12 minutes  total per watering day that's all your  grass needs run your sprinklers three  times a day four minutes each cycle with  about one hour space to part now if you  have a drip system you're watering your  plants you're watering trees you don't  need to operate your system every single  day in the summer set it to two to three  days a week all summer for one cycle of  30 to 90 minutes depending on the size  of your drip emitter  to learn more about how to water in the  summer some watering summer watering  tips you can visit  snwa.com waterways fines start at eighty  dollars and they can go up to twelve  hundred and eighty dollars for repeat  offenders  to avoid some really costly hefty fines  you know don't allow water to spray or  flow off your property follow the  mandatory seasonal watering restrictions  and fix and adjust broken sprinklers if  you see  water waste occurring in your  neighborhood in your community report it  to your local water provider water waste  is typically caused by inefficient or  improper landscape irrigation  to prevent waterways and to improve the  efficiency of your irrigation system you  can follow some simple steps and those  include checking your irrigation system  after you mow it for misaligned or  broken sprinklers  also  ensuring that your sprinkler heads are  the correct size or height for your  landscape also look for irrigation leaks  to learn more about how to prevent water  waste or to report waterways visit  snwa.com  and our thanks to the southern nevada  water authority for sponsoring this  segment you can get more water saving  tips by visiting  snwa.com or calling that phone number on  the screen 70258  save
 

